course: dictionary
lesson: 3913
title: Fritter: food and wasting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fritter is a noun, a thing you can eat. It is a piece of fruit, vegetable or meat dipped in batter and fried, like an apple fritter or a corn fritter. The clue is in the example: «syrnYky are fritters of soft cottage cheese, eaten with smetAna or jam», so a fritter can even be made from cheese.
explain: Fritter is also a verb, an action word. To fritter away time or money means to waste it little by little on unimportant things. Look at the words around it: pocket money, sweets, small things. Those clues tell you it is about wasting, not about food.
explain: Try the swap check. «Sam frittered away his pocket money on sweets he did not even like.» If you swap in "fried", the sentence makes no sense. Swap in "wasted little by little" and it fits.
fact: A fritter is food dipped in batter and fried.
fact: «Syrnyky» are fritters of soft cottage cheese, eaten with smetAna or jam; here «syr» means cheese.
fact: «Fritter away» means to waste time or money little by little on unimportant things.
fact: Food fritters you may meet: UK chip shops sell spam and pineapple fritters, New Zealand cooks make whitebait fritters, and Australians have potato fritters.
exercise: «Syrnyky are fritters of soft cottage cheese, eaten with smetAna or jam.» What is a fritter? | A jar of smetana | A cheese that has been left to melt | A sweet, sticky drink | *A piece of food dipped in batter and fried
exercise: «Sam frittered away his pocket money on sweets he did not even like.» What does frittered away mean here? | Saved carefully in a money box | *Wasted little by little on unimportant things | Given to his gran as a present | Fried in batter until golden
exercise: Mum says, «Let's make corn fritters for tea.» What are corn fritters? | Sweetcorn in a tin of soup | A pair of corn-coloured socks | *Corn mixed with batter and fried into small cakes | Popcorn sold at the cinema
test: Jaya says, «The chip shop sells pineapple fritters.» What is a pineapple fritter? | A pineapple cut into very thin slices | A small pineapple tree in a pot | Pineapple juice in a tall glass | *A piece of pineapple dipped in batter and fried
test: «We must not fritter our time away on silly games.» What does fritter away mean? | *To waste time little by little | To fry things quickly in hot oil | To run very fast | To save time for later
exam: In «Lily frittered her money away on tiny things», what does frittered away mean? | Counted carefully | Hidden in a drawer | *Wasted little by little | Fried in a pan
